# The arms model switch (#385.3): cfg vr_arms_model = classic (the only player choice since #466), the channel command
# `arms custom|arx`, and the hand size vr_hand_scale. status.json: vr.body.armsModel,
# vr.body.arxArmsHidden (true while the Arx arm faces are not drawn = custom; PROPOSED name, 385.3 implements it),
# vr.body.<hand>.handScale, vr.body.<hand>.custom.tipLength (palm to fingertip, units).
# The hand scale steps use the PROPOSED channel command `arms scale <factor>` (live vr_hand_scale, range 0.8 - 1.5);
# the channel has no generic live cfg set today.
# Needs the first-person save:
#   .\scripts\dev\xrs-run.ps1 arms-model
#   .\scripts\dev\smoke-test.ps1 -VrSim idle -Sequence arms-model -Save mvp-new-game
@sim idle
@save mvp-new-game
@args --loadslot 0

@until state eq GAMEPLAY 60s
@until vr.sim.timelineFrame ge 270 60s       # 3 s into the level: past its fade-in (TRAPS.md)
@assert player.controlsBlocked eq false
@assert vr.body.bound eq true
@assert vr.body.active eq true

vr-sim head rot 0 -40 0
vr-sim hand left off
vr-sim hand right pos 0.15 -0.3 -0.4
vr-sim hand right rot 0 0 0
@frames 15
@assert vr.body.right.posed eq true

# 1. The default is classic (the owner's pick, #466); the custom arms (test-only until #486 removes them) hide the
#    Arx arm faces
@assert vr.body.armsModel eq classic
@assert vr.body.arxArmsHidden eq false
arms custom
@frames 5
@assert vr.body.armsModel eq custom
@assert vr.body.arxArmsHidden eq true
@shot model-custom

# 2. The Arx arms: the faces are drawn again, the posed logical arm is unchanged
arms arx
@frames 5
@assert vr.body.armsModel eq arx
@assert vr.body.arxArmsHidden eq false
@assert vr.body.right.posed eq true
@shot model-arx

# 3. Back to custom
arms custom
@frames 5
@assert vr.body.armsModel eq custom
@assert vr.body.arxArmsHidden eq true

# 4. Both ways again (the hide mask survives the switch)
arms arx
@frames 3
@assert vr.body.armsModel eq arx
@assert vr.body.arxArmsHidden eq false
arms custom
@frames 3
@assert vr.body.armsModel eq custom
@assert vr.body.arxArmsHidden eq true

# 5. Hands bigger than the Arx hands by default (first proposal 1.15); the length grows with the setting
@assert vr.body.right.handScale gt 1.0
@assert vr.body.right.custom.tipLength gt 0
@remember tip0 vr.body.right.custom.tipLength
@remember scale0 vr.body.right.handScale
arms scale 1.4
@frames 5
@assert vr.body.right.handScale gt 1.35
@assert vr.body.right.handScale lt 1.45
@assert vr.body.right.handScale gt {scale0}
@assert vr.body.right.custom.tipLength gt {tip0}
@shot hand-scale-140
arms scale 1.0
@frames 5
@assert vr.body.right.handScale lt 1.05
@assert vr.body.right.custom.tipLength lt {tip0}
arms scale 1.15
@frames 5
@assert vr.body.right.handScale gt 1.1
@assert vr.body.right.handScale lt 1.2

@assert errors eq 0
